## The harbour square

::bg{location="harbour_square_market" time="morning"}
::music{playback="start" mood="festive" volume="normal"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: Saturdays, the square fills with trestle tables: peaches, smoked mackerel, second-hand anoraks, a man who sharpens anything for a pound.
::actor{character="ines" anchor="left" action="slideInLeft"}
::actor{character="theo" anchor="right" action="slideInRight"}
::set{run.seen.ines = run.day}
::set{run.seen.theo = run.day}
@ines{code="0010" emotion="surprised"}: Oh — hello.
@theo{code="0010" emotion="neutral"}: Morning.
@narrator{code="0020"}: They look at each other the way people do who went to the same tiny school and never once spoke.

<branch id="market" prompt="Pell asked for peaches. Who do you walk the stalls with?">
  <choice id="ines" text="Ines is looking at the book stall.">
    ::set{run.aff.ines += 1}
    ::actor{character="theo" action="slideOut"}
    @ines{code="0020" emotion="happy"}: Look — a 1962 tide almanac. Someone's grandfather wrote in all the margins.
    @ines{code="0030" emotion="shy"}: I'm buying it. I'm going to read every note. That's my whole Saturday. Want to hear the good ones?
  </choice>
  <choice id="theo" text="Theo is haggling over rope.">
    ::set{run.aff.theo += 1}
    ::actor{character="ines" action="slideOut"}
    @theo{code="0020" emotion="teasing"}: Watch. He'll say twelve, I'll say eight, we'll both say ten, and then he'll throw in a peach because he knew my dad.
    @narrator{code="0030"}: That is exactly what happens. Theo gives you the peach.
  </choice>
  <choice id="peaches" text="Just buy the peaches.">
    ::actor{character="ines" action="slideOut"}
    ::actor{character="theo" action="slideOut"}
    @narrator{code="0040"}: The peaches are warm from the sun and bruise if you look at them.
  </choice>
</branch>
